# The dashboard is authored on Windows and served to browsers from a Linux
# rover. Force LF in the working tree.
#
# WHY, AND WHY IT IS NOT COSMETIC HERE
# ====================================
# This is the third place in this repository to need this file. The rover tree
# got one after every payload file was found to be CRLF, which put a "\r" on
# the shebang of the script a systemd unit ExecStarts for the drive link -- and
# the resulting error names a file that plainly exists:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# For the dashboard the failure is quieter but the same shape: any .sh or
# .py helper here that ends up executed on the rover fails the same way, and a
# CRLF in a served .js is a byte-level difference that survives every visual
# inspection.
#
# `git ls-files --eol` is the check. `i/lf w/crlf attr/` means the committed
# bytes are fine and the WORKING TREE is not -- and the working tree is what
# gets copied into an image or served by a static file server.
*               text eol=lf

# Never touch binary payloads.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pgm           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.pdf           binary
*.rknn          binary
*.onnx          binary
